INT. NORTHSIDE SOUND - LIVE ROOM - NIGHT

ON CAMERA: handheld, shaky, a red REC dot in the corner. The mic stand fills the frame, then swings toward JUNIPER, 19, headphones around their neck, staring at a lyric sheet.

JUNIPER
(to camera)
This is take nineteen. They said twelve was fine. I said twelve was fine.

OSEI (O.S.)
Twelve was not fine.

The camera whips left. OSEI, 20s, engineer, hunched at the glass of the control room. A studio dog sleeps under his chair. A pizza guy hovers at the door with two boxes, unsure whether to knock.

OSEI (CONT'D)
You rushed the bridge.

JUNIPER
I didn't rush -- they're the one who

OSEI
-- you came in early on "stay" --

JUNIPER
-- because the click track is wrong, Osei, it's wrong, I told you --

A phone BUZZES on the console. Osei thumbs it. Speaker.

MARGUERITE (V.O.)
(tinny, over the phone)
Hi, babe, is it done? The label guy is asking.

JUNIPER
He's asking?

OSEI
Marguerite, not now --

MARGUERITE (V.O.)
-- he wants the single Friday, Juniper, they have a slot, and you promised --

JUNIPER
I never promised! You promised! You said I'd get to say when it's done!

Juniper rips the headphones off and hurls them. They CRACK against the glass. The dog bolts. The pizza guy backs out. The camera drops, tilts, catches the ceiling tiles, and cuts to black.
